flowchart TD
  Target["Target primitive: quantum P plus classical Q on secp256k1"]
  Algorithm["Algorithm"]
  Optimization["Optimization"]

  Target --> Algorithm
  Target --> Optimization

  %% Algorithm: the reversible point-add construction
  Phases["Affine P plus Q in eight in-place phases: x -= Qx, y -= Qy, y /= x gives lambda, x += 3Qx, x -= lambda squared, y *= x, y -= Qy, x = Qx - x; the x steps fused into the walk seed and unseed"]
  DivLeg["Division leg: y /= x by the forward Leapfrog walk, 156 ticks, payloads in place"]
  Square["Chained-row square in the 2^128 frame: x -= lambda squared; every carry chain runs to the full accumulator; wrap witness and REDC frame slide"]
  MulLeg["Multiplication leg: y *= x by the reversed walk; the tape is consumed"]
  Walk["Leapfrog walk: two odd signed rails; per tick two forced add-halves T = (T +- B)/2, one deep-or-flat choice add-halve from the low bits and a top-bit compare, 0-3 extra halvings by a barrel"]
  Tape["Tape: one 5-bit letter per tick; tick 0's letter re-derived at the end"]
  Cells["Payload cells: P_i = mu R_i mod p follows the letters; one-fold and merged add-halve cells, chunked modular adds with windowed boundary carries, flags and folds"]
  Cleanup["Cleanup: payloads coincide at the division endpoint and one is cleared; the reversed walk consumes the tape and restores the denominator; every phase returns scratch to zero"]
  Post["Exact post-passes: redundant CCX removal on product, affine, quadratic and truth supports, measurement absorption, conditional and classical-factor passes; 96-gate X identity tail"]

  Algorithm --> Phases
  Phases --> DivLeg
  Phases --> Square
  Phases --> MulLeg
  DivLeg --> Walk
  MulLeg --> Walk
  Walk --> Tape
  Walk --> Cells
  Tape --> Cleanup
  Cells --> Cleanup
  Square --> Cleanup
  Cleanup --> Post

  %% Optimization: score and reliability decisions
  Base["Base: spookyfrog 14, ecdsa.fail 1829986, 1,234 qubits x 755,314 Toffolis at about 19 failing shots per 9,024; walk rule, cells and formula kept"]
  Length["Walk length: 138 to 156 ticks; no-park tail below about 1e-8 per walk"]
  Widths["Width table: per tick the 2e-8 quantile of 110 million random walks plus 6 bits; 1 of 100 million further walks exceeds it"]
  Cap["Qubit cap 1,360: with the wider rows and longer tape, 1,350 does not fit (room of the one-fold tick 131)"]
  Windows["Windows: chunk-boundary compares +12, narrowed-compare table off; flag compares +12; merged folds 70; cell fold floor 72; one-fold fold +12; erase compares 40; fold guard 32"]
  SqExact["Square: exact carry tails, wrap witness 33 top bits, correction and REDC guard 36 bits, exact assembly tail"]
  JointOff["Multiplication joint low-fold shortcut off: its room-dependent finite low cut is replaced by the regular fold"]
  Unbound["Bound tables off: post-pass tables, allocator states and tick loans keyed to the base gate list"]
  Contract["Inherited contract: error only bought back, about 0.001 failure events per 9,024 shots, no error-for-score trade"]

